# Docs at the end of a change

When a feature, fix, or task is finished and it changes behavior, an API, payments, Rune XP, navigation, or a TODO/phase row, update the matching docs in that same turn. Do not wait for a separate "update the md files" request.

| What changed | Update |
|---|---|
| Shopper-visible behavior | `CHANGELOG.md` Unreleased. `README.md` if the feature list changed |
| How the live app works | `PROJECT_INSIGHTS.md`. `AI_AGENT_GUIDE.md` if the next agent would do the wrong thing |
| A TODO row or phase | `TODO.md` and `PROJECT_PROGRESS.md` |
| A new screen or API module | `DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md` table |
| Production-grade technique | Craft patterns in `PROJECT_INSIGHTS.md` (problem, approach, where; no git/PR badges) |

Skip docs when the product did not change: a question, commit-message lines, a typo, a rename, a reverted experiment, or the user said not to touch the docs.

```md
<!-- ❌ leave CHANGELOG saying cancel does not reverse XP after the refund path shipped -->
<!-- ✅ Unreleased note plus the TODO checkbox in the same turn the code lands -->
```
